- Story & Context: This legendary track serves as the final myth of the Kinderkrampf scene, chronicling the legend of the "Phantom Express"—a driverless freight train that supposedly roams the border tracks carrying the broken vocal synthesizers of deceased androids. Built around a hauntingly delicate, high-register bass melody that collides with a wall of tremolo black-metal guitars, the song ends with forty seconds of pure, un-amplified room acoustics where only the mechanical clicking of a bass pedal and distant wind can be heard. It is said that playing this track at midnight on any disused platform will cause the rails to hum with low-frequency gabber sub-bass. "Tell me if the track switches led to somewhere warm."
